{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Repair verification report\n\nProblem: _collect_node_ids launched a nested pytest collection process in the shared numbered temp root, allowing session cleanup to delete another run tree.\n\nProven root cause/proof: a collection-time plugin forced the real nested TempPathFactory to initialize against PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT with pytest-0..3. Without private basetemp, cleanup deleted the pytest-0 sentinel; supplying private basetemp preserved exact entries and bytes. Plain collect-only was a negative experiment because lazy temp initialization never fired.\n\nTest: held-out tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity_basetemp.py was RED before repair and is GREEN after. Removing exactly the --basetemp arguments returned it to RED; they were restored. The oracle also pins exact node parsing and unchanged shared-root entries.\n\nFix: _collect_node_ids owns a TemporaryDirectory and passes nested pytest a private --basetemp while preserving signature, selection, cwd, capture/text, timeout=300, accepted rc 0/5, and :: parsing.\n\nSafety/gates: parity suite plus oracle 23 passed; make lint and make typecheck passed. No dependency or user-facing capability added and no test weakened.\n\nSiblings/parity: bounded search found the previously fixed tests/_store_isolation.py pattern and no additional confirmed occurrence that initializes pytest temp state; other collect-only subprocesses do not by themselves trigger the mechanism. This is internal test infrastructure, so CLI/MCP/library parity slots are N/A.\n\nReplication: the original poisoned shared numbered-root scenario now preserves every preexisting entry and sentinel byte while returning the expected collected node."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787022567330428001,"uuid":"e34fc52b-d455-46ca-8026-66f6be47a599"}